X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Visitlancastercity": "https://visitlancastercity.com/event/songs-stories-of-the-american-revolution/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:visitlancastercity
X-SOURCE:Visit Lancaster City
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260419T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260419T153000
DTSTAMP:20260418T104050
CREATED:20260327T194131Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260327T194132Z
UID:57141-1776607200-1776612600@visitlancastercity.com
SUMMARY:Songs & Stories of the American Revolution
DESCRIPTION:Historic Rock Ford’s America250 Lecture Series presents “Songs and Stories of the American Revolution.” Dressed in Colonial garb\, presenter Matthew Dodd takes audiences back in time to the days of the American Colonial settlement and the American Revolution. Using rousing period songs and stories that put the songs into the context of the time\, Matthew brings to life the exciting Days of 1776.  Matthew sings and plays guitar\, banjo and mandolin. \n\n\n\nThis presentation will begin at 2 PM in the Langmuir Education Room located on the first floor of the Rock Ford Barn. Prior to the lecture\, attendees may visit the Snyder Gallery and our 2026 Focus Exhibit. The Snyder Gallery closes at 4 PM.  \n\n\n\nAbout the Presenter: Matthew Dodd is a retired teacher and now a full time musician. He does a great many history and holiday-themed shows.
URL:https://visitlancastercity.com/event/songs-stories-of-the-american-revolution/
LOCATION:Historic Rock Ford\, 881 Rockford Road\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17602\, United States
CATEGORIES:History,Music and Dance
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitlancastercity.com/wp-content/uploads/America250-Songs-and-Stories-.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Historic Rock Ford":MAILTO:office@HistoricRockFord.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancasterpa": "https://lancasterpa.com/events-calendar/folsom-prison-experience-american-music-theatre/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancasterpa
X-SOURCE:Discover Lancaster
