BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Visitlancastercity": "https://visitlancastercity.com/event/revolutionary-lancaster-lecture/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:visitlancastercity
X-SOURCE:Visit Lancaster City
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260420T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260420T210000
DTSTAMP:20260418T104050
CREATED:20260327T194314Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260327T194316Z
UID:57144-1776711600-1776718800@visitlancastercity.com
SUMMARY:Revolutionary Lancaster Lecture
DESCRIPTION:Historic Rock Ford’s America250 Lecture Series welcomes Benton G. Webber as he presents “Revolutionary Lancaster.” Lancaster County was not the site of any military battles of our country’s Revolutionary War\, but the community was impacted in almost every other way possible. Come and learn about life here 250 years ago and how it was turned upside down as “the course of human events” at the global and national scale came crashing down right here in Lancaster\, disrupting the lives of many in order to secure “certain unalienable rights.” \n\n\n\nThis presentation will begin at 7 PM in the Langmuir Education Room located on the first floor of the Rock Ford Barn. Admission is for the lecture only and does not include the Snyder Gallery.  
URL:https://visitlancastercity.com/event/revolutionary-lancaster-lecture/
LOCATION:Historic Rock Ford\, 881 Rockford Road\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17602\, United States
CATEGORIES:History
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitlancastercity.com/wp-content/uploads/America250-Revolutionary-Lancaster.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Historic Rock Ford":MAILTO:office@HistoricRockFord.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Saintjameslancaster": "https://www.saintjameslancaster.org/event/evening-compline-2-2/2026-04-20/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:saintjameslancaster
X-SOURCE:Saint James Lancaster
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260420T210000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260420T210000
DTSTAMP:20260419T232742
CREATED:20250102T152850Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20250105T190000Z
UID:10004001-1776718800-1776718800@www.saintjameslancaster.org
SUMMARY:Evening Compline
DESCRIPTION:Evening Compline\nvia Zoom\nClick here to join Compline. (This link can be used for every evening Compline on Zoom.) \n\nThe short service of Compline is based on the closing time of prayer in the Daily Office\, or monastic cycle of prayer. It is observed in monasteries around 8 or 9 PM when darkness has fallen and bedtime is near. \n\nThe thoughts that inspire the prayers during Compline are the need for divine forgiveness and protection against the powers of darkness. Prayers for peace and rest are offered as night falls. \n\nPeople of all faiths and beliefs are invited to this contemplative service. The service lasts about 20 minutes.
URL:https://www.saintjameslancaster.org/event/evening-compline-2-2/2026-04-20/
LOCATION:Saint James Episcopal Church\, 103 North Duke Street\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17602\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.saintjameslancaster.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/decorative-candles-cropped-250px.jpg
GEO:40.040058;-76.30344
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Saint James Episcopal Church 103 North Duke Street Lancaster PA 17602 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=103 North Duke Street:geo:-76.30344,40.040058
END:VEVENT
