UID:3682-1777662000-1777667400@www.lancastertrust.com
SUMMARY:the King will come Joined by the LBC Choir
DESCRIPTION:Sponsored by the Melva S. McIlwaine Guest Artist Endowment Fund \nThe King will come is a multi-denominational worship collective of songwriters\, musicians and creatives\, who turn personal stories into loving\, honest\, and vulnerable worship to God. These testimonies of struggle\, surrender\, redemption\, and divine grace are highlighted in their debut album “Conversations with God.” The collective is best known for the viral song\, “yet (don’t give up)\,” which has more than 38 million views on YouTube. \nThe King will come will be accompanied by the LBC Grand Chorus\, consisting of the Chamber Singers\, the Men’s Chorus and the Women’s Chorus\, and the Milton Hershey School Gospel Choir. LBC choral students will also have the opportunity to learn from the artists in the collective through an on-campus masterclass. \nReserve Your Tickets
URL:https://www.lancastertrust.com/community-events/the-king-will-come-joined-by-the-lbc-choir/
LOCATION:Lancaster Bible College’s Good Shepherd Chapel\, 901 Eden Road\, Lancaster\, 17601\, United States
END:VEVENT
